---
// MeetDetails (#4432): ported from the approved EnviousMeet mock-up.
---

<section class="s"><div class="wrap">
  <div class="s-head"><div><span class="eyebrow rule">Premium, without the price</span><h2>Premium details,<br><em>free for everyone.</em></h2></div>
  <p class="s-lede">Built for real calls: AirPods, mute buttons, people talking over each other, and meetings in a room. No paid plan, so nothing is locked.</p></div>
  <div class="spot">
    <div class="spot-tabs" id="spotTabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Premium details">
      <button type="button" role="tab" class="on" style="--c:var(--r1)"><i></i>Respects your muted mic</button>
      <button type="button" role="tab" style="--c:var(--r7)"><i></i>Real speaker names</button>
      <button type="button" role="tab" style="--c:var(--r5)"><i></i>Play back any moment</button>
      <button type="button" role="tab" style="--c:var(--r2)"><i></i>Synced with your calendar</button>
      <button type="button" role="tab" style="--c:var(--r9)"><i></i>No bot in your call</button>
      <button type="button" role="tab" style="--c:var(--r3)"><i></i>In-person meetings</button>
    </div>
    <div class="deck" id="deck">
      <div class="flip on" style="--c:var(--r1)"><div><h3>Respects your muted mic.</h3><p>Muting yourself in Zoom does not turn off your Mac&rsquo;s microphone. We designed EnviousMeet to follow your mute in the Zoom app, the Teams app and Google Meet in Chrome or Safari, so your side chatter stays out of the recording, transcript and summary. A few seconds around a mute change may be kept.</p></div><div class="vis" aria-hidden="true"><div class="sc sc-m2">
  <img class="m2-bg" src="/meetings/office.webp" alt="" width="720" height="530" decoding="async" loading="lazy">
  <div class="m2-lap"><div class="m2-scr">
    <div class="m2-tiles"><span><b>MC</b><small>Maya</small></span><span><b>LP</b><small>Leo</small></span><span class="you"><b>You</b><em class="m2-muted">MUTED</em></span></div>
    <div class="m2-bar"><i class="m2-mic"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round"><rect x="9" y="3" width="6" height="11" rx="3"/><path d="M5.5 11a6.5 6.5 0 0013 0M12 17.5V21"/><path class="m2-slash" d="M4 4l16 16"/></svg></i><i class="m2-cam"></i><i class="m2-end"></i></div>
  </div><div class="m2-base"></div></div>
  <div class="m2-vis"><img class="m2-idle" src="/meetings/visitor-idle.webp" alt="" width="185" height="460"><div class="m2-wave"></div></div>
  <img class="m2-w m2-back" src="/meetings/worker-back.webp" alt="" width="420" height="431" decoding="async" loading="lazy">
  <img class="m2-w m2-turn" src="/meetings/worker-turn.webp" alt="" width="420" height="431" decoding="async" loading="lazy">
  <b class="m2-b m2-b1">Got a sec?</b>
  <b class="m2-b m2-b2">Sure, one min!</b>
  <div class="m2-notes"><span class="m2-h">EnviousMeet notes</span>
    <div class="m2-l m2-l1"><b>Maya</b>Q3 numbers look good.</div>
    <div class="m2-l m2-l2"><mark>You were muted: side chat left out</mark></div>
    <div class="m2-l m2-l3"><b class="you">You</b>Sorry, I&rsquo;m back. Let&rsquo;s ship it.</div>
  </div>
</div></div></div>
      <div class="flip" style="--c:var(--r7)"><div><h3>Real speaker names.</h3><p>EnviousMeet picks up real names from Zoom, Teams and Google Meet, and it never guesses one. When the call sound has speech in it, your microphone is marked You, with or without headphones.</p></div><div class="vis" aria-hidden="true"><div class="sc sc-desk sc-nm"><svg viewBox="0 0 340 250" class="desk">
  <rect class="dk-wall" x="0" y="0" width="340" height="250"/>
  <rect x="10" y="10" width="320" height="108" rx="10" fill="#1b1530"/>
  <rect x="18" y="18" width="71" height="70" rx="7" fill="#2e2650"/><rect class="nm-ring nm-r0" x="18" y="18" width="71" height="70" rx="7"/><text x="53.5" y="54" class="dk-ini">MC</text><text x="53.5" y="76" class="dk-nm">Maya Chen</text><rect x="95" y="18" width="71" height="70" rx="7" fill="#2e2650"/><rect class="nm-ring nm-r1" x="95" y="18" width="71" height="70" rx="7"/><text x="130.5" y="54" class="dk-ini">LP</text><text x="130.5" y="76" class="dk-nm">Leo Park</text><rect x="172" y="18" width="71" height="70" rx="7" fill="#2e2650"/><rect class="nm-ring nm-r2" x="172" y="18" width="71" height="70" rx="7"/><text x="207.5" y="54" class="dk-ini">PS</text><text x="207.5" y="76" class="dk-nm">Priya Shah</text><rect x="249" y="18" width="71" height="70" rx="7" fill="#4a2f86"/><rect class="nm-ring nm-r3" x="249" y="18" width="71" height="70" rx="7"/><text x="284.5" y="54" class="dk-ini">You</text><text x="284.5" y="76" class="dk-nm">You</text>
  <circle cx="148" cy="103" r="7" fill="#3a3160"/><circle cx="170" cy="103" r="7" fill="#3a3160"/><rect x="186" y="97" width="28" height="12" rx="6" fill="#e23a55"/>
  <rect class="dk-notes" x="10" y="128" width="320" height="114" rx="12"/>
  <text x="24" y="148" class="dk-h">Transcript</text>
  <g class="nm-badge"><rect x="226" y="137" width="92" height="16" rx="8" fill="#efe6fd"/><text x="272" y="148.5" class="nm-bt">Names found</text></g>
  <g class="nm-line nm-w0"><text x="24" y="172" class="nm-lab nm-a">Speaker 1</text><text x="24" y="172" class="nm-lab nm-b c1">Maya Chen</text><text x="96" y="172" class="dk-l">Can we ship on Friday?</text></g><g class="nm-line nm-w1"><text x="24" y="192" class="nm-lab c3">You</text><text x="96" y="192" class="dk-l">Yes, if QA signs off.</text></g><g class="nm-line nm-w2"><text x="24" y="212" class="nm-lab nm-a">Speaker 2</text><text x="24" y="212" class="nm-lab nm-b c2">Leo Park</text><text x="96" y="212" class="dk-l">QA finishes today.</text></g><g class="nm-line nm-w3"><text x="24" y="232" class="nm-lab nm-a">Speaker 3</text><text x="24" y="232" class="nm-lab nm-b c4">Priya Shah</text><text x="96" y="232" class="dk-l">I'll tell support.</text></g>
</svg></div></div></div>
      <div class="flip" style="--c:var(--r5)"><div><h3>Hear any moment again.</h3><p>The audio stays on your Mac until you delete it. Every passage has a timestamp, and you can Transcribe again with another engine whenever you like.</p></div><div class="vis" aria-hidden="true"><div class="sc sc-desk sc-pb"><svg viewBox="0 0 340 250" class="desk">
  <rect class="dk-notes" x="0" y="0" width="340" height="250"/>
  <text x="20" y="28" class="pb-title">Q3 roadmap sync</text>
  <text x="20" y="43" class="pb-meta">Ready &#183; Parakeet &#183; 32 min, 10 sec &#183; Audio: 18 MB</text>
  <rect x="20" y="52" width="92" height="17" rx="5" class="pb-btn"/><text x="66" y="63.8" class="pb-bt">&#8635; Transcribe again</text>
  <rect x="117" y="52" width="66" height="17" rx="5" class="pb-btn"/><text x="150" y="63.8" class="pb-bt">Delete audio</text>
  <g class="pb-play"><path d="M21 77.5l7 4.5-7 4.5z" fill="#1d1d1f"/></g>
  <g class="pb-pause"><rect x="21" y="77.5" width="2.6" height="9" rx="1" fill="#1d1d1f"/><rect x="25.4" y="77.5" width="2.6" height="9" rx="1" fill="#1d1d1f"/></g>
  <rect x="38" y="80.5" width="200" height="3" rx="1.5" fill="#e4dff0"/>
  <rect class="pb-fill" x="38" y="80.5" width="200" height="3" rx="1.5" fill="#793bd4"/>
  <circle class="pb-thumb" cx="38" cy="82" r="5.5" fill="#fff" stroke="#cfc6e2"/>
  <text x="320" y="85" class="pb-clock pb-c1">3:10 / 32:10</text><text x="320" y="85" class="pb-clock pb-c2">12:04 / 32:10</text><text x="320" y="85" class="pb-clock pb-c3">12:07 / 32:10</text>
  <rect x="20" y="96" width="300" height="18" rx="6" fill="#efeaf6"/><rect x="22" y="98" width="98" height="14" rx="5" fill="#fff" class="pb-seg"/>
  <text x="71" y="108.3" class="pb-segt on">Transcript</text><text x="170" y="108.3" class="pb-segt">Notes</text><text x="270" y="108.3" class="pb-segt">Summary</text>
  <text x="20" y="136" class="pb-who">Maya Chen</text><text x="79" y="136" class="pb-t">3:10</text><circle cx="108" cy="132.8" r="5.2" fill="none" stroke="#793bd4" stroke-width="1.2"/><path d="M106.4 130.20000000000002l4 2.6-4 2.6z" fill="#793bd4"/><text x="20" y="151" class="pb-say">Let&rsquo;s start with the launch date.</text><text x="20" y="172" class="pb-who">Leo Park</text><text x="67" y="172" class="pb-t">12:04</text><circle cx="102" cy="168.8" r="5.2" fill="none" stroke="#793bd4" stroke-width="1.2"/><path d="M100.4 166.20000000000002l4 2.6-4 2.6z" fill="#793bd4"/><text x="20" y="187" class="pb-say">Support needs the help pages by Friday.</text><text x="20" y="208" class="pb-who">You</text><text x="45" y="208" class="pb-t">12:31</text><circle cx="80" cy="204.8" r="5.2" fill="none" stroke="#793bd4" stroke-width="1.2"/><path d="M78.4 202.20000000000002l4 2.6-4 2.6z" fill="#793bd4"/><text x="20" y="223" class="pb-say">I&rsquo;ll draft them tomorrow.</text>
  <g class="pb-cursor"><path d="M0 0v13l3.4-3.2 2.4 5.4 2.2-1-2.4-5.3H10z" fill="#1d1d1f" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="1"/></g>
  <circle class="pb-click" cx="0" cy="0" r="8"/>
</svg></div></div></div>
      <div class="flip" style="--c:var(--r2)"><div><h3>Meeting notes named from your calendar.</h3><p>Optional. Each meeting takes the title of your calendar event, so it is easy to find in History. EnviousMeet also saves who was invited. The calendar is only read, never changed.</p></div><div class="vis" aria-hidden="true"><div class="sc sc-cl2">
  <div class="c2-cal">
    <div class="c2-top"><b>Thursday, November 6</b><span>Today</span></div>
    <div class="c2-grid">
      <div class="c2-hr"><i>9 AM</i></div><div class="c2-hr"><i>10 AM</i></div><div class="c2-hr"><i>11 AM</i></div><div class="c2-hr"><i>12 PM</i></div>
      <div class="c2-ev"><b class="c2-hl">Q4 launch planning</b><small>10:00 to 10:30 AM</small><small>Maya Chen, Leo Park, Priya Shah</small></div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="c2-app">
    <div class="c2-bar"><i></i><i></i><i></i></div>
    <div class="c2-body">
      <div class="c2-side">
        <b class="c2-h">History</b>
        <div class="c2-seg"><span>A</span><span>D</span><span>T</span><span class="on">M</span></div>
        <div class="c2-row on"><small><em></em>Nov 6, 10:00 AM</small><b class="c2-hl">Q4 launch planning</b><div class="c2-pv">Maya: Can we ship on Friday? Leo: QA is done.</div><span class="c2-chips"><span>Meeting</span><span>30 min</span></span></div>
        <div class="c2-row"><small>Nov 5, 3:30 PM</small><b>Zoom call, Nov 5</b></div>
      </div>
      <div class="c2-main">
        <b class="c2-title c2-hl">Q4 launch planning</b>
        <div class="c2-inv">Invited: Maya Chen, Leo Park, Priya Shah</div>
        <div class="c2-tabs"><span>Transcript</span><span>Notes</span><span class="on">Summary</span></div>
        <b class="c2-sh">Key points</b>
        <ul><li>Launch moves to Friday, Nov 14.</li><li>QA finishes this week.</li></ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div></div></div>
      <div class="flip" style="--c:var(--r9)"><div><h3>Nobody sees a notetaker join.</h3><p>We skipped the meeting bot. EnviousMeet uses the Mac&rsquo;s own audio tools to record your microphone and the call sound directly, so the transcript starts from clean, first-hand audio. Call sound needs macOS 14.2 or later. Works with AirPods too.</p></div><div class="vis" aria-hidden="true"><div class="sc sc-kb">
  <div class="kb-floor"></div>
  <div class="kb-lap"><div class="kb-scr">
    <div class="kb-tiles"><span><b>MC</b></span><span><b>LP</b></span><span class="you"><b>You</b></span></div>
    <div class="kb-toast kb-ask"><i>&#129302;</i>Notetaker bot wants to join</div>
    <div class="kb-toast kb-ok"><i class="dot"></i>Recording on this Mac</div>
  </div><div class="kb-base"></div></div>
  <img class="kb-bot" src="/meetings/bot.webp" alt="" width="141" height="280" decoding="async" loading="lazy">
  <b class="kb-pow">BOOT!</b>
  <div class="kb-chibi"></div>
</div></div></div>
      <div class="flip" style="--c:var(--r3)"><div><h3>For the meeting in the room, too.</h3><p>Put your Mac on the table to record an in-person meeting. EnviousMeet tells voices apart and gives each one its own label, so you still see who said what. Start it from the menu bar.</p></div><div class="vis" aria-hidden="true"><div class="sc sc-r2"><div class="r2-art"><div class="r2-zoom"><img src="/meetings/room.webp" alt="" width="720" height="530" decoding="async" loading="lazy">
  <i class="r2-ring r2-k0" style="left:18.8%;top:30%;--c:#1e7ad6"></i><i class="r2-ring r2-k1" style="left:50%;top:33%;--c:#c4561b"></i><i class="r2-ring r2-k2" style="left:81%;top:35%;--c:#1f8a5b"></i><b class="r2-tag r2-k0" style="left:18.8%;top:19%;--c:#1e7ad6">Speaker 1</b><b class="r2-tag r2-k1" style="left:50%;top:22%;--c:#c4561b">Speaker 2</b><b class="r2-tag r2-k2" style="left:81%;top:24%;--c:#1f8a5b">Speaker 3</b>
  <i class="r2-rec" style="left:50%;top:75%"></i></div></div>
  <div class="r2-tx"><span class="r2-h">Transcript<em>&#9679; Recording</em></span><div class="r2-l r2-l0"><b style="color:#1e7ad6">Speaker 1</b>Let&rsquo;s review the new layout.</div><div class="r2-l r2-l1"><b style="color:#c4561b">Speaker 2</b>It tested well with users.</div><div class="r2-l r2-l2"><b style="color:#1f8a5b">Speaker 3</b>Great, let&rsquo;s ship it Friday.</div></div>
</div></div></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div></section>
